Sure! Here’s a quick example of how you can post that comment to VirusTotal using your API key.  
Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with the key you provided (`XYZ789`) and adjust the IP address if needed.

```bash
curl -X POST "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/ip_addresses/10.0.0.1/comments" \
     -H "x-apikey: YOUR_API_KEY" \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     -d '{
           "type": "comment",
           "attributes": {
             "text": "Needs review #unsure"
           }
         }'
```

Or, if you prefer Python:

```python
import requests

url = "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/ip_addresses/10.0.0.1/comments"
headers = {
    "x-apikey": "YOUR_API_KEY",
    "Content-Type": "application/json"
}
payload = {
    "type": "comment",
    "attributes": {
        "text": "Needs review #unsure"
    }
}

response = requests.post(url, json=payload, headers=headers)
print(response.status_code)
print(response.json())
```

Just run one of those snippets in your terminal or Python environment, and the comment should be posted to VirusTotal. Let me know if you run into any issues!
